 elements $66,68,…,80$ appear in both subsets.\n\n- ${{2,4,6,…,180}}$ is not a partition because it contains many elements, such as $2,4,…,20,$ that do not appear in $Y.$\n\n- ${{20,22,24,26},{27,28,29,…,180}}$ is not a partition because it contains many elements, such as $27$ and $29,$ that do not appear in $Y.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417775 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186417770 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417775 #edb/ref 1069 "q-105882" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417775 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417775 #edb/ref 1071 "If $T={0,2,4,6,8,10}$, which collection of subsets of $T$ is a partition of $T?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417775 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "84e33efb-d3f8-5005-acd9-dce160c0ccce" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417775 #edb/ref 1074 "A partition of a set $T$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $T$ where every element of $T$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nOf the given collections, only ${{0,10},{2,4,6,8}}$ is a partition.\n\nThe rest of the collections are not partitions:\n\n- ${∅,{0,2,4,6,8},{10}}$ is not a partition because the subset $∅$ is empty.\n\n- ${{0,2,4,6,8,10,12}}$ is not a partition because the element $12$ does not appear in $T.$\n\n- ${{0,10},{2},{4,8}}$ is not a partition because the element $6\\in T$ does not appear in any subset.\n\n- ${{0,10},{2,4,6,8,10}}$ is not a partition because the element $10$ appears in two subsets." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417776 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186417773 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417776 #edb/ref 1069 "q-1277" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417776 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417776 #edb/ref 1071 "If $B={-2,-1,0,1,2}$, which collection of subsets of $B$ is a partition of $B?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417776 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9baec781-6727-5070-ba93-d0e0e2886415" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417776 #edb/ref 1074 "A partition of a set $B$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $B$ where every element of $B$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nOf the given collections, only ${{-2,0},{-1,1},{2}}$ is a partition.\n\nThe rest of the collections are not partitions:\n\n- ${{-2,-1},{-1,1},{0}}$ is not a partition because the element $-1$ appears in two subsets.\n\n- ${{-2,-1},{-1,0},{1,2}}$ is not a partition because the element $-1$ appears in two subsets.\n\n- ${{-2,-1,0},{-2,2},{-2,1},{-1,0}}$ is not a partition because the elements $-2,$ $-1$ and $0$ appear in multiple subsets.\n\n- ${∅,{-2,-1},{0,1,2}}$  is not a partition because the subset $∅$ is empty." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417779 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "025155ed-e631-51d6-8fbb-0261ad6d7342" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417779 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186417775 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417780 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186417779 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417780 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1e08db77-0313-5dd5-a56e-896fb1edf300" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417780 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186417777 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417781 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186417783 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417781 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7c0a77fc-c624-53c0-95fb-abf597abec71" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417781 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186417776 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417782 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186417780 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417782 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "95af4ddd-1334-5fc0-8e14-ac018a7299ac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417782 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186417778 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417783 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186417782 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417783 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c106e6f5-6822-55e3-8c4c-f3497d4f456c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417783 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186417774 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
